    "title": "100 Year Old Murder Mystery Continues - NewsBreak",
    "text": "abc23.com\nwebsite\nCambria County, Pennsylvania\n100 Year Old Murder Mystery Continues\n10 hours ago\nThe mystery of where the bodies of 5 babies killed almost a hundred years ago are buried continues. On Tuesday, the Coroner said he’s expanding his investigation. Cambria County Coroner Jeff Lees led a team to exhume the bodies of 5 babies killed in the 1920’s and 30’s by their mother. Their mummified bodies were found in a trunk in Stella Williamson’s Gallitzin home in 1980, after her death. Skulls of two of the babies were recently found at a Museum in Philadelphia and returned to Lees for burial.\nComments\nLoading editor...",
